From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:53:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 134/138] media: apple: t7000 ISP: full-resolution stills
 (START flags, fw RAW buffer)

ISP_IOC_START takes preset-choice flags next to the camera number:
ISP_START_PHOTO_VIEW (smallest preset >= 640x480 with the full-res aspect:
rear 1632x1224 @60, front 1376x968 @60), ISP_START_STILL (full resolution:
rear 3264x2448, front 1376x968) and ISP_START_PRESET (an explicit index).
Bare 0/1 keep the old choice; older drivers reject the flags with EINVAL.

Full-res presets make the fw ask for a 48 MB RAW buffer ('0WAR' 0x2db887e);
we refused anything over 32 MB, so CH_START asserted
"CImageFlowH6.cpp, 2185: chEntryApple->icRawBufferOut != 0". SHAREDMALLOC
now honours up to 64 MB and reuses a freed surface of the same tag (the fw
re-allocates '0WAR' on every preset change); max_shared_mb defaults to 256.
IMX190 preset 3 (2592x1936) never delivers a frame and hangs the fw: skipped.

Knobs for experiments, off by default: raw_local (0x125
LOCAL_RAW_BUFFER_ENABLE; accepted, not what the assert wants) and raw_pool
(host buffers for the fw's RAW pool, type 3).

Verified on hw (oscar kernel): rear STILL 3264x2448 at 15 fps (dim scene),
PHOTO_VIEW rear 1632x1224 @59 fps, front 1376x968 @55 fps; '0WAR' reused on
the second STILL start.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
